<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 160,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 barley. [CORRECTED 14:10 GMT]</title>
<headline>Japan buys 160,000 tonnes wheat, 40,000 barley. [CORRECTED 14:10 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said it had bought 100,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 20,000 of Canadian wheat, 40,000 of Australian wheat, 20,000 of U.S. barley and 20,000 of Australian barley at its weekly tender on Thursday.</p>
<p>These are for January shipment. The tender details are as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 100,000	   Western white	    40,000</p>
<p>				    Dark northern spring   20,000</p>
<p>				    Hard red winter</p>
<p>				     (11.5 percent protein)20,000</p>
<p>				     (13 percent protein)  20,000</p>
<p> Canada	20,000	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>								   20,000</p>
<p> Australia   40,000	   Standard white	   40,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 20,000	    Feed			 20,000</p>
<p> Australia  20,000	    Feed			 20,000</p>
<p>(Corrects to Australia from Canada in table above)</p>
</text>
